An imported file is only used for exploring (atlas and historical explorer) during this session and always appears labelled as such. The forecasts, the lab and the comparison remain based on the official catalogue version
An atlas of the seismic activity recorded since {0} and a
A catalogue is an ordered list of earthquakes. Each row says when it happened, where, at what depth, with what magnitude and with how much uncertainty it was located. We use the public catalogue of the National Seismological Network of the Colombian Geological Survey.
A catalogue is never complete
One circle per event
The same event identifier appears more than once (for example, where queries overlap).
A model is calibrated if, when it says {0}%, the event happens about {1}% of the time.
A model is only justified if it improves on the historical-frequency baseline on data after its training, and if its probabilities are calibrated. When the improvement is small or unstable between blocks, the simpler model is preferred.
A real record from the catalogue
An isolated earthquake cannot be anticipated. What can be measured is how often a
A single colour
One page with the main figures and messages
A high probability of activity does not mean high risk, and vice versa. This platform estimates probability of activity; it does not compute risk.
A high probability indicates that earthquakes above the threshold are recorded often in that zone, as in the Bucaramanga nest, where activity is very deep and rarely causes damage. It says nothing about damage or an imminent event. Earthquake preparedness is advisable throughout the country, whatever the value on the map.
A high probability does not mean that an earthquake will certainly occur. A low probability does not mean a total absence of activity either.
A high probability does not mean that an earthquake will certainly occur. A low probability does not mean a total absence of activity either. The values express how often similar zone-periods recorded at least one event in the past; they do not indicate damage or an imminent event.
A probability of {0}% means that, of every {1} similar zone-periods in the past, about {2} recorded an event. It does not say which ones or when.
A probability of {0}% means that, of every {1} similar zone-periods, at least one event was observed in about {2}. It does not say in which. A high probability is not certainty and a low one is not absence of activity.
A probability of twenty per cent means that, of every hundred similar zone-periods, about twenty recorded an event. It does not say which. That is why each value is shown with its uncertainty interval.
